{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Because of this.</b> Rabbi Marinus said: the meaning of בעבור זה is that it should have been inverted: זה בעבור שעשה ה' לי, and he brought many like it for his opinion. In my view, none of them is correct, for how can we invert the words of the living Elohim? And the meaning of the verse is the reverse of what he thought, for we do not eat matzot 'because of this'; rather, 'because of this' means because of this service, which is the eating of matzah. And he shall not eat hametz — it is the first of the commandments that HaShem commanded us — [that] HaShem performed signs for us until He brought us out of Egypt. And the reason He brought us out of Egypt was only to serve Him, as written: 'When you bring the people out of Egypt you shall serve Elohim on this mountain' (above, Exodus 3:12), and as written: 'who brought you out of the land of Egypt to be Elohim to you' (Numbers 15:41)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "Resolved למעלה ג יב as a cross-reference to Exodus 3:12 within the same book; במד' טו מא resolved as Numbers 15:41."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:08.555407011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}